  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Linear equations, systems, and inequalities form the largest tested domain on the EST I. Fluency here is non-negotiable for a high score.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Lines & systems",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Slope-intercept form: \\( y = mx + b \\). Slope: \\( m = \\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} \\). Solve systems by substitution or elimination. For inequalities, flip the sign when multiplying or dividing by a negative.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Slope-intercept",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( y=mx+b \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Point-slope",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( y-y_1=m(x-x_1) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Absolute value",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( |x-a|=b \\Rightarrow x=a\\pm b \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Slope",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( m=\\dfrac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve: \\( 2(3x-1)=5x+4 \\). \\[ 6x-2=5x+4 \\implies x=6. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve the system: \\( 2x+y=7 \\), \\( x-y=2 \\). <p>Adding: \\( 3x=9 \\), so \\( x=3 \\), \\( y=1 \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "<h3>Linear inequalities</h3>A linear inequality such as \\( 2x-3 > 7 \\) is solved like an equation, but the solution is a range: \\( x > 5 \\). On a number line, use an open circle for strict inequalities (\\( > \\), \\( < \\)) and a closed circle for \\( \\geq \\) or \\( \\leq \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Solve the system: \\(3x + 2y = 16\\) and \\(x - y = 2\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "From second equation: \\(x = y+2\\). Substitute: \\(3(y+2)+2y=16 \\Rightarrow 5y=10 \\Rightarrow y=2, x=4\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
